    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0606" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg522"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Sir
                            M. H. Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have your letter of
                    the 18th of June, acknowledging receipt of mine of the 16th, and calling
                    attention to certain points in which our recollections of conversations seem not
                    exactly to agree. I take note of your corrections, which do not seem in any
                    essential point to affect the action of the two Governments in the case, and am,
                    my dear Sir Michael,</p>
                <p>Very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
